  10          /*
  11            
  12            This is a simple program that controls the robot. The algorithm does not remember the route, 
  13            it can only find an exit located on the perimeter of the maze, it cannot find the exit 
  14            inside the maze, that's why you must design a maze which contains the exit around it, or in a corner.
  15            You can change the values or limits according to your robot (in case you have designed your own).
  16            
  17            Requirements:
  18            
  19            According to my design, you must connect a battery that provides the robot with a voltage between 6.8 V a
             -nd 8 V.
  20            If you put less voltage, the robot will not work correctly or even it will not work.
  21            If you want to upload your own firmware, make sure to disconnect the jumper which supplies voltage to the
             - microcontroller. 
  22            I recommend following these steps.
  23            
  24            1. Open the project's output folder, it contains the .hex file.
  25            2. Select the STC89C52RC microcontroller.
  26            3. Disconnect the microcontroller power jumper and press the RESET button.
  27            4. Click the "Download/Program" button.
  28            5. Connect the power supply jumper again and realase the RESET button very quickly, and wait until the fi
             -rmware has been uploaded successfully.
  29            
  30          */
  31          
